WEBVTT

00:19:59.522 --> 00:20:00.698
EG: Yes.

00:20:00.722 --> 00:20:02.367
CA: That's an amazing thing to do,

00:20:02.391 --> 00:20:05.431
because those things will
quite probably live on after you,

00:20:05.455 --> 00:20:08.929
and they can literally rewire
many other people's minds.

00:20:08.953 --> 00:20:14.001
EG: Yeah, and I think we could call
your view of it "secular magic."

00:20:14.025 --> 00:20:16.177
CA: That's a great phrase.
I'll go with that.

00:20:16.201 --> 00:20:18.651
EG: Because the feeling
that you seem to get from it

00:20:18.675 --> 00:20:21.104
is exactly the same
as the feeling I get from it,

00:20:21.128 --> 00:20:23.640
which is: it is awfully exciting
to be a human being.

00:20:23.664 --> 00:20:29.006
And it is awfully exciting to be
permitted to dance and tiptoe

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:31.281
and engage and work